{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/printsLeger","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether leger lines are printed. Notes without leger lines indicate indeterminate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"high and low notes. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"; ignored for rests."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"printsLeger","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"print-leger"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/printsleger"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"printsLeger","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"printsLeger","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV11printsLegerSbvp"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/printsLeger":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether leger lines are printed. Notes without leger lines indicate indeterminate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"high and low notes. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"; ignored for rests."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/printsleger","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"printsLeger","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"printsLeger","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/printsLeger"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNote","abstract":[{"text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"}}}